of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}=-2{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=-3{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-2{b}_{2}+5{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-2{b}_{2}-\\frac{5}{3}(-3{b}_{1}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}-\\frac{5}{3}{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-66650074-ff68-5eca-a6ce-c53f9965f0b5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-66650074-ff68-5eca-a6ce-c53f9965f0b5" :answer-field/id #uuid "66650074-ff68-5eca-a6ce-c53f9965f0b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f9547433-2214-505b-b38c-379846b86b1e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4acab282-04ec-5eb0-ae3a-7ab839526ee4" "answer-ad9fccc8-89c8-5084-95ed-898b492b9317" "answer-f9547433-2214-505b-b38c-379846b86b1e" "answer-f26fb59e-92cb-5f2d-bb4b-31538da03416" "answer-af3b103c-e7ac-56f6-8025-6eee882f5637"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4acab282-04ec-5eb0-ae3a-7ab839526ee4" :answer/id #uuid "4acab282-04ec-5eb0-ae3a-7ab839526ee4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad9fccc8-89c8-5084-95ed-898b492b9317" :answer/id #uuid "ad9fccc8-89c8-5084-95ed-898b492b9317" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9547433-2214-505b-b38c-379846b86b1e" :answer/id #uuid "f9547433-2214-505b-b38c-379846b86b1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f26fb59e-92cb-5f2d-bb4b-31538da03416" :answer/id #uuid "f26fb59e-92cb-5f2d-bb4b-31538da03416" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af3b103c-e7ac-56f6-8025-6eee882f5637" :answer/id #uuid "af3b103c-e7ac-56f6-8025-6eee882f5637" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-be777f36-f8c5-5b1e-a52c-750939157337" :question/id #uuid "be777f36-f8c5-5b1e-a52c-750939157337" :question/math-academy-id "q-112714" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}},$ where ${c}_{1}=\\frac{3}{4}{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=4{b}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}-8{b}_{2}+3{b}_{3} \\\\  & =3{b}_{3}+2{b}_{1}-8{b}_{2} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}(\\frac{3}{4}{b}_{3})-2\\cdot 3(-\\frac{1}{3}{b}_{1})-2(4{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}-6{c}_{2}-2{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8e3da469-e9f0-5633-adf1-397b5dc595e3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8e3da469-e9f0-5633-adf1-397b5dc595e3" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e3da469-e9f0-5633-adf1-397b5dc595e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a59b9759-c63d-5d7d-b9fb-807706aa26b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d39fe87d-731d-5acb-a1d7-f42cd2ffa87d" "answer-d55d14b4-d250-5859-896a-6dd5a43d9894" "answer-506dc288-02b9-55d3-a86e-0b1ffd046ff9" "answer-a59b9759-c63d-5d7d-b9fb-807706aa26b0" "answer-f5598eb7-94b1-52af-8038-2d49b5545e84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d39fe87d-731d-5acb-a1d7-f42cd2ffa87d" :answer/id #uuid "d39fe87d-731d-5acb-a1d7-f42cd2ffa87d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d55d14b4-d250-5859-896a-6dd5a43d9894" :answer/id #uuid "d55d14b4-d250-5859-896a-6dd5a43d9894" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-506dc288-02b9-55d3-a86e-0b1ffd046ff9" :answer/id #uuid "506dc288-02b9-55d3-a86e-0b1ffd046ff9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a59b9759-c63d-5d7d-b9fb-807706aa26b0" :answer/id #uuid "a59b9759-c63d-5d7d-b9fb-807706aa26b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5598eb7-94b1-52af-8038-2d49b5545e84" :answer/id #uuid "f5598eb7-94b1-52af-8038-2d49b5545e84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120362 :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}},$ where ${c}_{1}=3{b}_{2}$, ${c}_{2}=-{b}_{3}$ and ${c}_{3}=4{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-3{b}_{1}+4{b}_{2}-6{b}_{3} \\\\  & =4{b}_{2}-6{b}_{3}-3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}(3{b}_{2})+6(-{b}_{3})-\\frac{3}{4}(4{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{c}_{1}+6{c}_{2}-\\frac{3}{4}{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 6 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-de484491-607f-5712-bf20-9fe92c23a765"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-de484491-607f-5712-bf20-9fe92c23a765" :answer-field/id #uuid "de484491-607f-5712-bf20-9fe92c23a765" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-65ce31d1-a577-5b44-a7fa-3c3f399d7aa4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fe8e8b08-4548-5fe8-adbd-3bce3207c85e" "answer-252cd9d2-cd28-51d0-86dc-f100bfbf8425" "answer-e15510ae-a912-51f2-b92f-d981d02b25f9" "answer-b63f4cd2-57fd-5205-92b4-a5bf14cc8ff8" "answer-65ce31d1-a577-5b44-a7fa-3c3f399d7aa4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe8e8b08-4548-5fe8-adbd-3bce3207c85e" :answer/id #uuid "fe8e8b08-4548-5fe8-adbd-3bce3207c85e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 6 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-252cd9d2-cd28-51d0-86dc-f100bfbf8425" :answer/id #uuid "252cd9d2-cd28-51d0-86dc-f100bfbf8425" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e15510ae-a912-51f2-b92f-d981d02b25f9" :answer/id #uuid "e15510ae-a912-51f2-b92f-d981d02b25f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b63f4cd2-57fd-5205-92b4-a5bf14cc8ff8" :answer/id #uuid "b63f4cd2-57fd-5205-92b4-a5bf14cc8ff8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 6 \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65ce31d1-a577-5b44-a7fa-3c3f399d7aa4" :answer/id #uuid "65ce31d1-a577-5b44-a7fa-3c3f399d7aa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 6 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-07f1e9fd-ac52-515f-8ec2-7b10b57c07ec" :question/id #uuid "07f1e9fd-ac52-515f-8ec2-7b10b57c07ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-113095" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{2}-{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}=-{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. Adding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}={b}_{1}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}={c}_{1}+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=2({c}_{1}+{c}_{2})-{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}={c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =4({c}_{1}+{c}_{2})-2({c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}+4{c}_{2}-2{c}_{1}-4{c}_{2} \\\\  & =2{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6f810d6a-b71d-5aa6-a732-e9b3cdb4d3fc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6f810d6a-b71d-5aa6-a732-e9b3cdb4d3fc" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f810d6a-b71d-5aa6-a732-e9b3cdb4d3fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1c013c9c-5216-521c-878e-e22df5716d0f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b20f4407-028f-5333-8613-ef2137552c30" "answer-94609691-7cfa-58f9-b339-110e2b9cb3d1" "answer-db1d9153-b78b-548a-ae9b-7d2f2545ca63" "answer-7b46227a-c88c-5619-8cec-a1c99318b271" "answer-1c013c9c-5216-521c-878e-e22df5716d0f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b20f4407-028f-5333-8613-ef2137552c30" :answer/id #uuid "b20f4407-028f-5333-8613-ef2137552c30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94609691-7cfa-58f9-b339-110e2b9cb3d1" :answer/id #uuid "94609691-7cfa-58f9-b339-110e2b9cb3d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db1d9153-b78b-548a-ae9b-7d2f2545ca63" :answer/id #uuid "db1d9153-b78b-548a-ae9b-7d2f2545ca63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b46227a-c88c-5619-8cec-a1c99318b271" :answer/id #uuid "7b46227a-c88c-5619-8cec-a1c99318b271" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c013c9c-5216-521c-878e-e22df5716d0f" :answer/id #uuid "1c013c9c-5216-521c-878e-e22df5716d0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f46f0e34-3d5c-5e7a-9fb4-690993802dbe" :question/id #uuid "f46f0e34-3d5c-5e7a-9fb4-690993802dbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-81230" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{2}-{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{2}-{b}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. By adding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=2{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}={b}_{1}+(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2})\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =7{b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\  & =7(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2})+(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{7}{2}{c}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2} \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d8e25391-7c4e-5c7c-8ae1-5b47ead04007"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d8e25391-7c4e-5c7c-8ae1-5b47ead04007" :answer-field/id #uuid "d8e25391-7c4e-5c7c-8ae1-5b47ead04007" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-20bb3464-f73d-5921-8cdf-f112ab14ead9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7f7a28ee-dddd-5aff-9301-8500542e8d7c" "answer-d1ea2e8b-285d-5d4a-86b6-3118e3eacc94" "answer-20bb3464-f73d-5921-8cdf-f112ab14ead9" "answer-36299c18-1f12-5691-a4cc-cf600875d435" "answer-e5b40102-f333-5f07-9467-4d1fb5ba690a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f7a28ee-dddd-5aff-9301-8500542e8d7c" :answer/id #uuid "7f7a28ee-dddd-5aff-9301-8500542e8d7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1ea2e8b-285d-5d4a-86b6-3118e3eacc94" :answer/id #uuid "d1ea2e8b-285d-5d4a-86b6-3118e3eacc94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20bb3464-f73d-5921-8cdf-f112ab14ead9" :answer/id #uuid "20bb3464-f73d-5921-8cdf-f112ab14ead9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36299c18-1f12-5691-a4cc-cf600875d435" :answer/id #uuid "36299c18-1f12-5691-a4cc-cf600875d435" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e5b40102-f333-5f07-9467-4d1fb5ba690a" :answer/id #uuid "e5b40102-f333-5f07-9467-4d1fb5ba690a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121043 :tutorial/content "Let's consider the basis $\\mathcal{C}= \\left\\{ \\mathbf{c}_1, \\mathbf{c}_2 \\right\\}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ and the vector\n\n![](images/2d/2dabd318dc49628f9333642f06492d3303617a0ea1cade93c0470c7a767121f5.svg)\n\nNow, let $\\mathcal{B}= \\left\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\right\\}$ be another basis of $\\mathbb{R}^2,$ such that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b}_1 = \\mathbf{c}_2 \\quad \\textrm{and} \\quad \\mathbf{b}_2 = -2\\mathbf{c}_1.\n$$\n\nHow can we find the coordinates of $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}?$\n\nSince ![](images/3e/3e330c07260a16bc76853ca1d275bbd9759f60179dce22500ee6dd38f326ca20.svg) we can write the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal B$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} \\\\  & =-{c}_{2}+2{c}_{1} \\\\  & =-({c}_{2})-(-2{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =-{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/5d/5d39ae32e2bad5125e6d7cf8ba7b943f2c926e1f1d6525ce019fd9a40c263bce.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121070 :tutorial/content "Let $\\mathcal{B}= \\left\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\right\\}$ be a basis of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ and ![](images/be/bec3577dd261660f2545adb66b9c26fbb520ea60aa6b0337094347dbc1937ff4.svg) What are the coordinates of $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{C}= \\left\\{ \\mathbf{c}_1, \\mathbf{c}_2 \\right\\},$ where $\\mathbf{b}_1 = 2\\mathbf{c}_1-\\mathbf{c}_2$ and $\\mathbf{b}_2 = \\mathbf{c}_1+\\mathbf{c}_2?$\n\nSince ![](images/20/200509c629fdf3d263ff375722f57ed77012a8a91a58a7e7f507fad3765b3782.svg) we can write the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ in terms of the vectors $\\mathbf c_1$ and $\\mathbf c_2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =5(2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2})-2({c}_{1}+{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =10{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2}-2{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2} \\\\  & =8{c}_{1}-7{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/6b/6bc09e66faaef40bba491f31c9342d4d08a8fb6eb3fd4dd1a3e2acdd77421741.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120055 :activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
